Behaviours:
Desktop feed enforcement:
- Bake the normalized allowed update repository into packaged metadata and inspect app-update.yml and Electron's active feed override before checking, downloading or installing updates.
- Restrict configured builds to the expected GitHub repository, host, protocol and latest channel; reject malformed, duplicate, missing, generic and foreign feeds, including mock-feed bypasses, and recheck around asynchronous installation.
- Publish refusal state and reasons to local and remote callers; keep Settings, sidebar update controls and update-everything consistent with disabled or refused updates.
- Preserve upstream server delegation of desktop-managed updates to the shell. Standalone server, CLI, SSH download and shared release behavior remain upstream.

Client release discovery and recovery:
- Bake the client release repository into desktop and web bundles. Resolve desktop startup recovery/reinstall links locally in the shell, without altering server-imported shared helpers.
- Use fork release-history links for renderer boot-failure downloads and tagged release links for update details; keep stock stable/nightly downloads in unconfigured clients.
- Discover configured web publication and release tracks through paginated fork GitHub releases, excluding drafts and preserving stable/nightly/preview selection, without official npm fallback for missing or malformed fork releases. Unconfigured clients keep upstream discovery.
- Refuse pinned-out local and remote desktop channel switches while retaining upstream expected-version guards, update recovery and cross-track database safety.

Fork release pipeline:
- Add a manually dispatched workflow restricted to chomamateusz/t3code, validating unused/increasing fork versions, resolving the source ref and supporting drafts and per-version concurrency.
- Require macOS signing inputs and reuse desktop release packaging for signed macOS arm64 and Linux x64 artifacts with fork feeds and desktop allowlists.
- Verify signatures, notarization, stapling, packaged AppImage/deb feeds and metadata, update manifests and CLI archive presence; publish artifacts and archive checksums. CLI archives retain upstream update behavior.

Integration details:
- Keep upstream managed update policy in force. Configured forks also refuse generic managed mirror feeds; fork checks bypass the new server npm-registry RPC, while unconfigured clients retain that RPC and its environment selection. The removed global publication check in update-everything remains removed; per-server delegation and guarded shell actions stay upstream. Track-switch missing-release copy names the configured repository.
- The upstream ManagedPolicy startup-recovery offer (#30319) composes with startupRecoveryReleaseUrl: Reinstall and Releases open the configured fork's releases.

Port to 965ddc1d6c:
- Applied without conflicts. Upstream #33142 added a Linux packaging-tool cache step to release-desktop.yml; the fork repository env lines are unchanged beside it. Upstream #33150 and #33153 install the t3 command from npx t3 and the desktop app; they add no desktop or web update feed or release endpoint, and CLI updates stay upstream.

Port to e07585e5fb:
- Upstream added its own apps/desktop/src/electron/ElectronUpdater.test.ts (#29672, AppImage relaunch without inherited descriptors). The feed-snapshot case moved into that file and spies on the real autoUpdater.setFeedURL instead of mocking electron-updater, so the upstream AppImage case keeps the real updater.
- DesktopUpdates.ts: the configured-fork "latest" channel pin now sits after #30804's canInstallUpdates flag; the install-time feed recheck follows #35018's parallel backend stop and SSH tunnel close. Upstream's 4-hour polling (#28481), stalled-download timeout (#26244), track-save fallback (#34917), AppImage cleanup (#29672, #36306) and T3 home lock fix (#26191) are kept unchanged around the guards.
- SettingsPanels.tsx: the About download button uses upstream's downloadLocalUpdate, which already reports getDesktopUpdateActionError, so a refused fork feed still shows "Could not download update".
- forkFeedPolicy.test.ts: a refused install now runs after upstream #35018 closed the SSH port forwards next to stopping the backends, so the recorded install steps are closeSshTunnels then startBackend, the same recovery upstream's failed install records.

